{"unit":25,"section":2,"cefr":"A1","objective":"use the possessive","skill":"Possessives 2","heading":"Use the possessive","phrases":[{"he":"הוא אבינו.","en":"He is our father.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/cadfae72bc8ac353d078b342246f0000","tokens":[{"w":"הוא","h":["(he) is","he","(it) is"]},{"w":"אבינו","h":["our father"]}]},{"he":"את ילדתי.","en":"You are my daughter.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/b6d1e30bf8d8b62d1754b8211b912992","tokens":[{"w":"את","h":["you"]},{"w":"ילדתי","h":["my girl"]}]},{"he":"כלביה רצים אליה.","en":"Her dogs run towards her.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/7f09fdce0fce17d5b457d8ad7dd85cbe","tokens":[{"w":"כלביה","h":["her dogs"]},{"w":"רצים","h":["are running","running","run"]},{"w":"אליה","h":["to her","towards her"]}]},{"he":"אחרי העבודה היא לובשת את שמלתה הלבנה.","en":"After work she wears her white dress.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/4469c390137db7ead5b1d3c600dd0f75","tokens":[{"w":"אחרי","h":["after"]},{"w":"העבודה","h":["the work","the job"]},{"w":"היא","h":["she","her","it"]},{"w":"לובשת","h":["wears","is wearing","wear"]},{"w":"את","h":["you"]},{"w":"שמלתה","h":["her dress"]},{"w":"הלבנה","h":["white"]}]}],"sentences":[{"he":"את ילדתי.","en":"You are my girl.","alt":[],"t":"l","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/b6d1e30bf8d8b62d1754b8211b912992"},{"he":"זאת אמנו.","en":"This is our mother.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ילדו שמח.","en":"His boy is happy.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הוא אביכם!","en":"He is your father!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הוא אבינו.","en":"He is our father.","alt":[],"t":"l","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/cadfae72bc8ac353d078b342246f0000"},{"he":"כלבה אוכל.","en":"Her dog is eating.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כלבם הולך.","en":"Their dog is walking.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"זאת אמי באה.","en":"That is my mother coming.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אמה של הילדה.","en":"The mother of the girl.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"חולצתי רטובה.","en":"My shirt is wet.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"מי אתה ילדִי?","en":"Who are you my child?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ילדיהם גבוהים.","en":"Their children are tall.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כלבִי לא מדבר.","en":"My dog doesn't speak.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"מסעדותיה ריקות.","en":"Her restaurants are empty.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"סוסךְ אוכל גזר.","en":"Your horse is eating a carrot.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כלביה רצים אליה.","en":"Her dogs are running to her.","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/7f09fdce0fce17d5b457d8ad7dd85cbe"},{"he":"כלבתה אוכלת הכל!","en":"Her female dog eats everything!","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"כלבתי שותָה מים.","en":"My female dog is drinking water.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"חולצתנו לא ורודה.","en":"Our shirt is not pink.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"ילדתו אוהבת אותו.","en":"His girl loves him.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כלביה ישנים הרבה.","en":"Her dogs sleep a lot.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כלבינו רצים בחוץ.","en":"Our dogs are running outside.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"ציפוריכם לא שרות.","en":"Your birds do not sing.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כל חולצותיי חדשות.","en":"All my shirts are new.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הסוסים רצים אלייך.","en":"The horses are running to you.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"הוא סוגר את מסעדתו.","en":"He is closing his restaurant.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ציפורייך שותות מים.","en":"Your birds are drinking water.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"היא מוכרת את חולצתו.","en":"She is selling his shirt.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"המלצר עומד על שמלתה.","en":"The waiter is standing on her dress.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כלבתנו שונאת חתולים.","en":"Our dog hates cats.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"אתה ילדִי ואני אביךָ.","en":"You are my boy and I am your father.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"זאת מסעדתי או מסעדתו?","en":"Is it my restaurant or his restaurant?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ציפוריי שומעות אותךָ.","en":"My birds hear you.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ילדותיי הן ילדותייךָ.","en":"My girls are your girls.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"סוסנו אוכל כי הוא רעב.","en":"Our horse is eating because it is hungry.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אפילו סוסִי יודע את זה!","en":"Even my horse knows this!","alt":["Even my horse knows that."],"t":"t"},{"he":"חולצותיו של הגבר יבשות.","en":"The man's shirts are dry.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הם מתפללים אחרי העבודה.","en":"They are praying after the work.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"האם ילדתכן אוהבת ממתקים?","en":"Does your girl love sweets?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אנחנו צופים בילדים רצים.","en":"We watch the children run.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"אני נותנת לאמךְ את שמלתךְ.","en":"I am giving your mother your dress.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ילדיו של הרופא רוצים עוגה.","en":"The doctor's children want cake.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"ילדותיו אוכלות אך ורק פסטה.","en":"His girls eat nothing but pasta.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"כלביהם של הגברים שותים מים.","en":"The men's dogs are drinking water.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"למה אתם מוכרים את מסעדותיכם?","en":"Why are you selling your restaurants?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אני אוהבת אתכן, ילדותיי היפות.","en":"I love you, my pretty girls.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אנחנו פותחים את מסעדתנו רק בערב.","en":"We open our restaurant only in the evening.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אחרי העבודה היא לובשת את שמלתה הלבנה.","en":"After work she wears her white dress.","alt":[],"t":"l","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/4469c390137db7ead5b1d3c600dd0f75"},{"he":"חולצותיהם היפות של הילדים יותר מדי קטנות עליהם.","en":"The children's pretty shirts are too small on them.","alt":[],"t":"l"}],"hints":{"את":"it / that / the fruit","ילדתי":"my girl","זאת":"it is (feminine) / that / that is (feminine)","שמח":"happy (sg. masc.) / happy / happy (m.s)","הוא":"(he) is / (it) is / he","אבינו":"our father","כלבה":"dog","אוכל":"eat / eating / eats","הולך":"walk, go (m.s - pres.) / walk, go","באה":"come / comes / is coming","של":"'s / Abraham's / avraham's","הילדה":"the girl / the girl is","מי":"the one who / who / who are","אתה":"you / you are / you (m.s)","לא":"aren't / didn't / do not","מדבר":"speak / speaks / talks","גזר":"a carrot / carrot","כלביה":"her dogs","רצים":"are running / run / running","אליה":"to her / towards her","אוכלת":"are eating / eating / is eating","הכל":"all / everything / everything, all","שותָה":"drink / drinking / drinks","מים":"water","אוהבת":"like / likes / love","אותו":"him / it / the same","הרבה":"a lot of / lots of / many","בחוץ":"outside","שרות":"are singing / sing","כל":"all / all of / each","חדשות":"new / news (n) / news","היא":"her / it / she","על":"about / at / by","שמלתה":"her dress","חתולים":"cat / cats","ואני":"and I / and I am","או":"or","אותךָ":"you / thee, you (m.s) / thee, you (f.s)","הן":"are / they / they are","כי":"because","רעב":"hungry (m.s)","אפילו":"even","יודע":"know / knows","זה":"it / it is / it's","הגבר":"the man / the man is","יבשות":"continent","הם":"are / they / they are","אחרי":"after / after I / after (Prep)","העבודה":"the job / the work","האם":"do / does / is","ממתקים":"candy","אנחנו":"we / we are / we (c.p)","בילדים":"her boys / her children / in boys","אני":"I / I am / I am a girl","רוצים":"do you want / want / want (m.p - pres.)","עוגה":"a cake / cake","אוכלות":"are eating / eat / eating","אך":"but / but, however, nevertheless","פסטה":"pasta","שותים":"are drinking / drink / drinking","למה":"why / why?","אתם":"do you want / you / you are","אתכן":"you (f.p)","רק":"just / only","בערב":"in the evening","לובשת":"is wearing / wear / wears","הלבנה":"white","הילדים":"the boys / the children / the kids","יותר":"any longer / any more / more","מדי":"much / too / too many"},"words":[{"he":"הלבנה","en":"white","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"אבינו","en":"our father","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"ילדתי","en":"my girl","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"כלביה","en":"her dogs","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"רצים","en":"run","alt":["are running","running"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"אליה","en":"towards her","alt":["to her"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"העבודה","en":"the job","alt":["the work"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"לובשת","en":"wears","alt":["is wearing","wear"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"loveshet"},{"he":"שמלתה","en":"her dress","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"כלבה","en":"Dog","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"kal'bah"},{"he":"הוא","en":"he","alt":["(he) is","(it) is"],"from":"phrase","tr":"hu"},{"he":"את","en":"you","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"at"},{"he":"אחרי","en":"after","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"akharei"},{"he":"היא","en":"she","alt":["her","it"],"from":"phrase","tr":"hi"}],"lexemes":["כלבינו","ילדותיי","כלבתה","חולצותיי","ציפורייך","חולצתו","כלבתי","ילדותייךָ","חולצתנו","ציפוריכם","כלביהם","מסעדתנו","ילדיהם","אבינו","סוסִי","אביכם","מסעדותיו","ילדתי","כלבה","כלבִי","ילדיו","ילדתו","מסעדותיה","סוסנו","סוסךְ","שמלתךְ","אביךָ","מסעדתי","מסעדתו","כלבם","ילדתכן","מסעדותיכם","ילדינו","שמלתה"],"tips":"Possessive nouns\n------------\n\nInstead of using \"של\" (see Possessives 1), every noun in Hebrew can also express a possessive connection by declining using the Hebrew genitive case. This form is usually used in formal speech and less likely to be used in normal daily language where we usually use the word \"של\", although certain words (family, body parts) are commonly used in this form in daily usage.\n\nFor this example we will use the noun \"סוס\" (a horse):\n\nEnglish Singular | Hebrew Singular | English Plural | Hebrew Plural\n---|---|---|---\nMy horse | סו**סִי** (sus**i**) | My horses | סו**סָיי**(sus**ai**)\nYour (s.m.) horse | סו**סְךָ** (sus**cha**) | Your(s.m.) horses | סו**סֶיךָ** (sus**echa**)\nYour (s.f.) horse | סו**סֶךְ** (sus**ech**) | Your(s.f.) horses | סו**סַיךְ** (sus**aich**)\nHis horse | סוס**וֹ** (sus**o**) | His horses | סו**סָיו** (sus**av**)\nHer horse | סו**סָהּ** (sus**a**) | Her horses | סו**סֶיה** (sus**e(h)a**)\nOur horse | ּסו**סֵנו** (sus**enu**) | Our horses | סו**סֵינוּ** (sus**enu**) \nYour (p.m.) horse | סו**סְכֶם** (sus**chem**) | Your(p.m.) horses | סו**סֵיכֶם** (sus**echem**)\nYour (p.f.) horse | סו**סְכֶן** (sus**chen**) | Your(p.f.) horses | סו**סֵיכֶן** (sus**echen**)\nTheir (m) horse | סו**סָם** (sus**am**) | Their(masucline horses | סו**סֵיהֶם** (sus**ehem**) \nTheir (f) horse | סו**סָן** (sus**an**) | Their(feminine) horses | סו**סֵיהֶן** (sus**ehen**)\n\nThis table might seem a little confusing, but once you try it a few times you'll get used to it! Moreover, you can see that the ending of the singular nouns are the same as the conjugations of the word \"של\", and in order to make a singular possessive noun into a plural possessive noun, we simply add the letter \"י\" before the ending.\n\nFor example :\n> סוס + ךָ (Your (s.m.) horse).\n\n> סוס + **י** + ךָ (Your (s.m.) horse**s**).\n\nWhen words have possessive endings attached to them, they are always definite, so when in an object position, they must be preceded by את:\n\nאני רואה **את** סוסך  \nI (can) see your horse."}